I don't think you can make GDSM/SDSM less attractive by boosting other colors,
unless you make them seem "too powerful".  Magic protection is an essential
for the game, and reflection is nearly so.  The only other sources of magic
protection are the cloak, which most non-wizards would also have to wish for,
and which competes with cloaks of displacement or with robes, or some
artifacts, which are stealable, unless you wish for someone else's Quest
artifact.  Reflection is easier to get, which is why most non-wizards go for
GDSM, but still takes valuable amulet or hand slots.  

In game balance terms magic protection and reflection are already almost "too
powerful".  But given that they exist it's a no-brainer to go for them.

>> White dragon scales: Amphibiousness.

A minor luxury; it's easy to never touch water.

>> Orange dragon scales: Free action.

That's more tempting.

>> Black dragon scales: Level-drain resistance and hallucination resistance. 

Wearing a CoMR or a robe means you don't really care about level-drain
resistance, and hallucination resistance is no big deal with unicorn horns or
blind telepathy.  (Or does telepathy hallucinate too?)

